<p>Adding or deleting a file changes the list of <a href="{{ path('uebertool_docs_pages.page', { slug: 'entrypoints' }) }}">entrypoints</a> and therefore the libraries. In dev mode the plugin takes care of it.</p>

<h2>What happens</h2>
<p>When a <code>.css</code>, <code>.js</code>, <code>.ts</code> or <code>.twig</code> file is <strong>added or removed</strong> (not when one changes), the plugin waits 500&nbsp;ms, then:</p>
<ol>
  <li>restarts the Vite dev server, which writes a fresh <code>libraries.yml</code>,</li>
  <li>runs the cache clear command, <code>drush cr</code> by default, so Drupal picks up the new libraries and templates.</li>
</ol>
<p>Files starting with an underscore are ignored.</p>

<h2>Configuration</h2>
{% embed code_block with { lang: 'ts', title: 'vite.config.ts' } %}{% block code %}{% verbatim %}
uebertool({
  features: {
    // Any command, split on spaces. `false` disables it.
    clearCache: 'ddev drush cr',
  },
})
{% endverbatim %}{% endblock %}{% endembed %}

{% embed aside %}
  {% block content %}
    <p>The command runs where Vite runs. If Vite runs on your host and Drupal in DDEV, use <code>ddev drush cr</code>.</p>
  {% endblock %}
{% endembed %}
